            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0761" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/143: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-27T20:00:00-05:00">September 27,
                            1939—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Your 196, September 26, 11 a.m.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d800-f1"/> The whole
                    shipping question is in abeyance pending the outcome of the Congressional
                    consideration of the neutrality question. We had a preliminary and informal
                    conversation with the British regarding trade with neutral countries about 2
                    weeks ago but, following the receipt of the British blockade note, it became
                    necessary to review the whole situation from the standpoint of our trade before
                    resuming the conversations. This review has now been completed and we expect to
                    make in the next day or so an oral statement to the British and to the
                    diplomatic representatives here of several neutral governments including the
                    Netherlands. We shall send you the substance of this statement as soon as <pb
                        facs="0762" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/> it is made. You may communicate the
                    foregoing to the Foreign Minister in the strictest confidence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d800-f1" n="40" xml:id="d800-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see telegram No. 176, September 15, 5 p.m., from the Minister in
                    the Netherlands, <ref target="#pg735">p. 735</ref>.</p>
